    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0176" n="162" xml:id="pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">790.00/11–3050</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. John Foster Dulles </hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d87-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-11-30">November 30,
                        1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Between my morning and afternoon meetings with Senators Taft<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d87-f2"/> and Millikin,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d87-f3"/> I jotted down
                    the enclosed notes which I read to Millikin and Taft in the afternoon,
                    indicative of my own initial reactions to the Korean developments.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d87-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John Foster Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d87-a1.xml" xpointer="d87-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d87-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d87-f1-content">
                <p>Consultant to the Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d87-f2" n="2" xml:id="d87-f2-content">
                <p>Senator Robert A. Taft of Ohio.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d87-f3" n="3" xml:id="d87-f3-content">
                <p>Senator Eugene D. Millikin of Colorado.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d87-f4" n="4" xml:id="d87-f4-content">
                <p>During the last week in November, United Nations forces advancing toward the Yalu
                    River were driven back by Chinese Communist counterattacks: for documentation on
                    Chinese intervention in the Korean War, see volume <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >vii</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
